---
title: "An agent keeps an R active binding in a named scope"
output: rmarkdown::html_vignette
vignette: >
  %\VignetteIndexEntry{An agent keeps an R active binding in a named scope}
  %\VignetteEngine{knitr::rmarkdown}
  %\VignetteEncoding{UTF-8}
---

This precomputed case exercises the endpoint's named scopes. Each scope is its
own persistent environment, `scopes` lists their objects without evaluating an
active binding, and `reset` empties one scope while the others keep theirs.
Returned scalars travel as Arrow IPC and are decoded by ducknng inside the
fresh DuckDB client.

```{pi, provider="openai-codex", model="gpt-5.4", thinking="medium", timeout=900, extension="./extensions/pi-ducknng/index.ts"}
Using the package tools, start the R adapter and follow its ducknng manifest. With eval in scope `analysis`, install a read-only active binding `mean_mpg` in `environment()` whose getter returns `mean(datasets::mtcars$mpg)`. With eval in the default scope, set `cars <- nrow(datasets::mtcars)` and return `exists("mean_mpg")`. In a fresh eval in scope `analysis`, return `mean_mpg`. Call scopes and note the class it reports for `mean_mpg`. Reset scope `analysis`, then return `exists("mean_mpg")` from scope `analysis` and `cars` from the default scope. Close the endpoint. Report the default scope's `exists` result, the decoded mean, the reported class, both post-reset results, and the endpoint process identity, beginning with `AGENT_VERIFIED_ACTIVE_BINDING` only when all calls succeed.
```
